Used in: tools/k-labor/lib/prose/generic-pack.json
  15 entries of skills/humanize-korean/references/lexicon.json (v1.3, tier "change"):
  AST-38, AST-39, AST-42, AST-48, AST-56, AST-57, AST-61, L-12, L-13, L-17,
  L-23, L-25, L-26, L-27, X-04. The narrow "regex" and "regex_exclude" fields are
  copied unchanged, except L-17: "(?<![가-힣])" is prepended so that long Hangul
  runs stay linear time. That prefix alone would miss a match that starts right
  where the previous match ended inside a Hangul run, so the entry also carries
  the unchanged upstream regex as "resume", and the runner retries it at exactly
  that position. The combined result equals the upstream regex.
  Headwords appear in the "fix" text. The exclude window (12 code points around
  each candidate) follows scripts/lexical_layer.py, but within one line only.
  Grades, reasons and output policy are ours.
No code from im-not-ai is copied; the rule runner (tools/k-labor/lib/prose/check.mjs) is new.
The packaged npm release carries the same notice in tools/k-labor/THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md.
